---
// The workspace's packages and their dependencies, drawn from the manifests as the site builds,
// so the diagram is never out of date. Each section's packages are drawn inside its box. Drawn with Starlight's colour variables so it follows the
// light and dark themes.
import { BOX_HEIGHT, BOX_WIDTH, dependencyGraph } from "./dependency-graph.ts";

const graph = dependencyGraph();
import Diagram from "./Diagram.astro";
---

<Diagram title="Workspace package dependencies" minWidth={900}>
  <svg
    viewBox={`0 0 ${graph.width.toFixed(0)} ${graph.height.toFixed(0)}`}
    style={`max-width: ${graph.width.toFixed(0)}px`}
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="dependencies-title dependencies-desc"
  >
    <title id="dependencies-title">Workspace package dependencies</title>
    <desc id="dependencies-desc">{graph.description}</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker
        id="dependencies-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="head"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    {
      graph.sections.map((section) => (
        <g>
          <rect
            class="section"
            x={section.x.toFixed(1)}
            y={section.y.toFixed(1)}
            width={section.width.toFixed(1)}
            height={section.height.toFixed(1)}
            rx="10"
          />
          <text
            class="section-title"
            x={(section.x + 14).toFixed(1)}
            y={(section.y + 28).toFixed(1)}
          >
            {section.title}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))
    }
    {
      graph.lines.map((line) => (
        <path class:list={["line", { dev: line.dev }]} d={line.path}>
          <title>{`${line.from} → ${line.to}`}</title>
        </path>
      ))
    }
    {
      graph.boxes.map((box) => (
        <g>
          <rect
            class:list={["box", { published: box.published }]}
            x={box.x.toFixed(1)}
            y={box.y.toFixed(1)}
            width={BOX_WIDTH}
            height={BOX_HEIGHT}
            rx="6"
          />
          <text class="name" x={(box.x + 12).toFixed(1)} y={(box.y + 20).toFixed(1)}>
            {box.name}
          </text>
          <text class="directory" x={(box.x + 12).toFixed(1)} y={(box.y + 36).toFixed(1)}>
            {box.directory}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))
    }
  </svg>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Each package sits above what it depends on, in its section. Every gateway is drawn as one box,
    and every driver as another, since each has the same shape. An arrow is left out where another
    dependency already reaches the package. A dashed arrow is a dev dependency only. A highlighted
    package is in the <code>@govuk-once/</code> scope. Any package may use
    <code>@repo/utils</code> and <code>@repo/cloudfront-js-utils</code>, so no arrow is drawn to
    either. The shared ESLint, TypeScript and Vitest configuration, which every package uses, is
    left out, and so is this site.
  </Fragment>
</Diagram>

<style>
  .box {
    fill: var(--sl-color-bg);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }
  .box.published {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    marker-end: url(#dependencies-arrow);
  }
  .line.dev {
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }
  /* As Starlight resolves its own: --sl-font-mono is only set to override the system font. */
  .name,
  .directory {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono, var(--sl-font-system-mono));
  }
  .name {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .directory {
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
</style>
